    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Ennis Sisters 30th Anniversary"
      },
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "The Ennis Sisters 30e anniversaire"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Ennis Sisters are a Juno Award-winning trio hailing from St. John’s, Newfoundland & Labrador. They have been captivating audiences worldwide for over 25 years with their seamless harmonies and compelling songwriting. Flavoured by Celtic and traditional Newfoundland influences, their music offers a broad mix of original songs as well as uniquely interpreted tunes and ballads. In 1997, Maureen, Karen and Teresa Ennis took their first steps into the spotlight with the release of their debut album, Red is the Rose. This recording not only marked the beginning of their musical career but also showcased their innate talent and deep-rooted connection to the folk traditions of their home. They have since released 14 full-length studio albums and have earned numerous accolades along the way, including a prestigious Juno Award, a SOCAN award and multiple ECMAs and MusicNL awards. Throughout their career, they have embarked on extensive tours, taking them to stages across the globe, thrilling audiences with their powerful performances and leaving an indelible mark on the international music landscape. Their songs often reflect the resilience and warmth of the Newfoundland spirit, creating a meaningful connection with their listeners. As proud cultural ambassadors, The Ennis Sisters continue to enchant audiences with their timeless music, proving that the melodies of Newfoundland & Labrador can resonate and echo across the world. Their musical journey remains an enduring testament to the power of family, tradition, and the universal language of music."
      },
      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "The Ennis Sisters, trio primé aux Juno originaire de St. John’s, à Terre-Neuve-et-Labrador, enchante le monde entier depuis 25 ans avec ses harmonies irrésistibles et ses chansons évocatrices. Inspiré des traditions celtiques et terre-neuviennes, le groupe propose un savant mélange de chansons originales, de morceaux revisités et de ballades aux interprétations singulières. C’est en 1997, avec la parution de Red is the Rose, leur premier album, que Maureen, Karen et Teresa Ennis font une entrée remarquée sur la scène musicale canadienne. Ce premier enregistrement, véritable point de départ de leur carrière, laisse déjà entrevoir leur talent naturel et leur attachement profond aux traditions folk de leur terre natale qui deviendront leur signature. Depuis, elles ont signé 14 albums studio et remporté de nombreuses distinctions, dont un prestigieux prix Juno, un prix de la SOCAN et plusieurs prix MusicNL et de la musique de la côte est. Partout où elles se produisent, elles laissent derrière elles des salles conquises et des publics profondément touchés. Dans chacune de leurs chansons résonnent la ténacité et l’âme chaleureuse de Terre-Neuve; une authenticité qui touche le public droit au cœur. Fières de leurs racines, les trois sœurs font voyager l’âme de Terre-Neuve-et-Labrador bien au-delà de l’Atlantique grâce à une musique intemporelle. Bien plus qu’un trio folk, The Ennis Sisters incarne la force de la famille, la transmission des traditions et le pouvoir universel de la musique."
      }
    ]
  },
